# {{.Name}}

A fullscreen Twind app: a sidebar, cards, a dialog and a light and dark theme picker, styled with Tailwind classes and twi/ui components.

    go run .                                    run it: t picks the theme, tab moves focus, enter opens, q quits
    go tool twind dev .                         run it and swap in a new build on every save, styles included
    go test ./...                               check the styles are fresh and replay testdata/demo.twd
    go tool twind drive testdata/demo.twd       write each frame of the script to frames/

`go run . -theme Dark` opens in the dark theme.

## Styles

`twir_gen.go` holds the Style IR compiled from the Tailwind classes in this package and the twi/ui components it imports. It is committed, so the app builds with the Go toolchain alone. After changing a class, `go tool twind build` regenerates it (`twind dev` does so on every save), and `go tool twind check` says whether it is stale. Tailwind is not needed to build: it runs only to regenerate, from `.twind/bin/` in this or a parent directory, or else from the user cache (`%LocalAppData%\twind\tailwind\<version>` on Windows, `~/.cache/twind/tailwind/<version>` on Linux, `~/Library/Caches/twind/tailwind/<version>` on macOS), fetched there once from the Tailwind release and checked against the pinned sha256.

## Before the first Twind release

Twind has no published version yet. Point the module at a checkout:

    go mod edit -replace github.com/pehcastro/twind=../twind
    go mod tidy
